T626	Claim 79736 79766	So far, it is only a beginning
T627	Premise 80416 80472	By 1980 that same person was $500 below the poverty line
T628	Premise 80256 80346	In 1980 -- or 1979, a person with a fixed income of $8,000 was $500 above the poverty line
T629	Claim 80352 80414	this maybe explains why there are the numbers still in poverty
T630	Premise 80170 80254	Personal earnings after taxes per capita have gone up almost $3,000 in these 4 years
T631	Premise 80137 80168	Today it is up a plus 4 percent
T632	Premise 79944 80022	In the first half of 1980, gross national product was down a minus 3.7 percent
T633	Premise 80024 80068	The first half of '84 it's up 8\1/2\ percent
T634	Premise 80070 80135	Productivity in the first half of 1980 was down a minus 2 percent
T635	Claim 80512 80588	With regard to business investment, it is higher than it has been since 1949
T636	Claim 80594 80645	there seems to be no shortage of investment capital
T637	Claim 81125 81171	Today we're well on our way to a 600-ship navy
T638	Premise 80945 81020	back then we had planes that couldn't fly for lack of spare parts or pilots
T639	Premise 81022 81123	We had navy vessels that couldn't leave harbor because of lack of crew or, again, lack of spare parts
T640	Claim 81173 81195	We have 543 at present
T641	Claim 81197 81240	We have -- our military, the morale is high
T642	Claim 81856 82002	I think that we're in a position once again to heed the words of Thomas Paine, who said: "We have it in our power to begin the world over again.''
T643	Claim 82512 82546	That's what the economists tell us
T644	Claim 82469 82510	if you're modest income, you're worse off
T645	Claim 82373 82409	if you're wealthy, you're better off
T646	Claim 82411 82463	If you're middle income, you're about where you were
T647	Premise 83648 83730	when we sought to assault Social Security and Medicare, as the record shows we did
T648	Claim 83732 83762	I think that was mean-spirited
T649	Claim 84011 84036	America is a fair society
T650	Claim 84042 84132	it is not right that Vice President Bush pays less in taxes than the janitor who helps him
T651	Premise 84725 84795	this world is more complex and we're being pressed harder all the time
T652	Premise 84863 84946	we've had civil rights laws and the laws that prohibit discrimination against women
T653	Claim 84825 84844	We won the Olympics
T654	Claim 85034 85060	The question is our future
T655	Claim 84991 85032	The President's record is quite different
T656	Claim 85164 85309	We can be better if we face our future, rejoice in our strengths, face our problems, and by solving them, build a better society for our children
T657	Premise 85062 85163	President Kennedy once said in response to similar arguments, "We are great, but we can be greater.''
